infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Tuning maxReceiveCount: two ways to get it wrong
  desc The recommended window is 5–10 retries; either extreme has its own failure mode
  compares
    - label Too low (1–2)
      children
        - label Transient failures land in the DLQ
          desc Flaky downstream or a brief DB timeout looks like a poison pill
        - label Almost everything quarantines
          desc Most transient errors clear on the 2nd or 3rd attempt — you never give them one
        - label On-call drowns in false alarms
          desc Every transient becomes a poison-pill investigation
    - label Too high
      children
        - label Real poison pills thrash for a long time
          desc A consistently-crashing payload is retried over and over before quarantine
        - label Resources burned on doomed work
          desc Each redelivery re-runs the consumer that will crash again
        - label Source queue stays clogged
          desc Progress on healthy messages stalls behind the poison pill
theme
  palette #f43f5e #f59e0b
